(7651863, 1245048, 123833, '<td valign="top">Is it allowed to fly drones in the middle of the city? I thought there were some regulations forbidding it. I assumed this was taken from a high rise.<br/> <br/>Congrats on TT and leading the Unofficial Race.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2020-01-29 01:10:49.</i></td>', 'Is it allowed to fly drones in the middle of the city? I thought there were some regulations forbidding it. I assumed this was taken from a high rise. Congrats on TT and leading the Unofficial Race.', '2020-01-29 01:09:47.000000', '2020-01-29 01:10:49.000000', 0),
(7651873, 1244963, 250302, '<td valign="top">I''m so chuffed (learning the UK lingo) to have won first place with this photo.  Thank you so much for your votes and the blue ribbon!!!  This was our first day in Iceland (after a 7 hour delay departing London, and getting into bed at 2am).  We received word they were closing the mountain we had to cross to get to our Airbnb at 11am so we left Reykjavik early to ensure we made it before the roads closed.  As you can see it was grey skies with snow/sleet the whole way (and the winds, oh my!).  As we came into Vik I told my husband "that''s the church I want a photo of" and he immediately turned and climbed the hill to the church.  The clouds were so low and the compositions just weren''t working for me.  So I told him "it''s ok we''ll try again when we come back through."  He pulled over to this side parking lot and turned the car around so I was facing the church.  I said "YES!"  I saw what many of you commented on -- the red roof against the lack of color in the rest of the shot, the church with the stormy seas/jagged rocks in the background, the lights on in the church in the midst of the storm, and yes that pile of dirt that is distracting (Lol!).  A little detail extractor was able to bring out the detail in the clouds because they were quite flat and gray to the eye.  It''s my favorite photo from our 4 days in Iceland, and now to win a blue ribbon just makes it even better!!</td>', 'I''m so chuffed (learning the UK lingo) to have won first place with this photo.  Thank you so much for your votes and the blue ribbon!!!  This was our first day in Iceland (after a 7 hour delay departing London, and getting into bed at 2am).  We received word they were closing the mountain we had to cross to get to our Airbnb at 11am so we left Reykjavik early to ensure we made it before the roads closed.  As you can see it was grey skies with snow/sleet the whole way (and the winds, oh my!).  As we came into Vik I told my husband "that''s the church I want a photo of" and he immediately turned and climbed the hill to the church.  The clouds were so low and the compositions just weren''t working for me.  So I told him "it''s ok we''ll try again when we come back through."  He pulled over to this side parking lot and turned the car around so I was facing the church.  I said "YES!"  I saw what many of you commented on -- the red roof against the lack of color in the rest of the shot, the church with the stormy seas/jagged rocks in the background, the lights on in the church in the midst of the storm, and yes that pile of dirt that is distracting (Lol!).  A little detail extractor was able to bring out the detail in the clouds because they were quite flat and gray to the eye.  It''s my favorite photo from our 4 days in Iceland, and now to win a blue ribbon just makes it even better!!', '2020-01-29 04:52:10.000000', NULL, 0),
